From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:42:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] ci: scheduled macOS OS-marked test lane on the mini
 (non-required)

CI's tests-os lane is `if: false` in this fork (no GitHub-hosted macOS/Windows
runner), so outside tests/hermes_state/ and the six Native memory paths no
platforms("macos")/platforms("posix") test ever ran on Darwin in CI; macOS
proof was manual per card (e.g. PR #2390's fsync tests, run by hand on mbp).

Decision (kanban t_01a1d5b9382b24ad, option B): run tests-os.yml's macOS
selection on a schedule, not on PRs, and keep it out of the required gate.

.github/workflows/macos-os-tests.yml:
- schedule 00:37 and 12:37 UTC, workflow_dispatch, push macos-os-probe/**
  (not ci-probe/**, which also starts the hermes_state lane on the same runner);
- `gate` job on Linux runs scripts/ci/macos_os_tests_gate.py: a scheduled slot
  is skipped while any job for the mini's `hermes-state` label is waiting for a
  runner (queued/waiting/pending/requested); a job already running there is not
  a reason to skip. Dispatch/probe runs are never gated; an unreadable API
  fails open to testing. Job lists are read 8 in parallel (serial took ~3 min
  at 100+ open runs; parallel 34 s, live probe 2026-11-13 20:5x UTC: skipped,
  2 mini jobs waiting);
- test job on [self-hosted, macOS, hermes-state]: list_os_marked_tests.py macos
  (589 files today) -> run_tests.sh --files-from -j 2 under taskpolicy utility,
  `-m "platforms and not integration"`, throwaway HERMES_HOME; empty selection
  fails.

Red runs are meant to alert via the hub's ci_main_watch SCHEDULED set (state
branch; follow-up card adds the entry). ci.yaml gets a pointer comment above
tests-os (its `if: false  # fork: ...` line is untouched: fork-ci-runner.sh and
tests/ci/conftest.py match it). README: ci.yaml job table, Scheduled monitors,
full index.

Tests: tests/ci/test_macos_os_tests_workflow.py (workflow shape: no PR trigger,
not called by ci.yaml, gate wiring, mini labels, selection command; gate:
skips on each waiting status, runs when mini jobs only run or other labels
wait, excludes its own run and reads each run once, never gates dispatch/push,
fails open on CalledProcessError/TimeoutExpired/ValueError, writes run=false).
hermes-core-wt test: 7 files (new + fast/fork runner routing, job graph,
fork OS-lane hook, clean worktree, artifact quota) 83 passed.
scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks ok.
